WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:01.868
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:03.100
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.767
Thank you for being here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:04.767 --> 00:00:07.868
[ Cheering and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:07.868 --> 00:00:09.267
♪♪

00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:13.567
This weekend was
Easter, Passover, and Ramadan.

00:00:13.567 --> 00:00:15.200
It's what's known
in the religious community

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.400
as a Holy Turducken.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:19.701
I do love Easter Sunday, though.

00:00:19.701 --> 00:00:22.033
It's the day parents give
their kids a basket of candy

00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:23.667
then tell them
to sit quietly at church.

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:25.667
It's just very interesting.

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:27.734
Speaking of Easter,
today the Bidens hosted

00:00:27.734 --> 00:00:29.767
the first White House
Easter Egg Roll

00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:31.300
since the pandemic began,

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:32.400
and it was a huge event

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:35.667
with 30,000 people
in attendance.

00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:38.534
Yep, after two minutes
of rolling eggs across the lawn,

00:00:38.534 --> 00:00:40.234
the kids were like,
"Wow, I actually miss Zoom."

00:00:40.234 --> 00:00:43.467
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.467 --> 00:00:45.300
Meanwhile,
I was thrilled to be invited

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.567
and attend this year's
Easter Egg Roll.

00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:48.667
I did. I was there.

00:00:48.667 --> 00:00:49.501
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:49.501 --> 00:00:52.567
Today. This morning.

00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:54.400
I told President Biden
it was an honor

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.367
and a privilege to be there
and he said, "Uh, Jimmy,

00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:57.868
we invited 30,000 people."

00:00:57.868 --> 00:01:00.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.868
But I actually did get to go
to the White House today, yeah.

00:01:02.868 --> 00:01:07.000
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.434
When they said, "The president
wants to see you,"

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:11.634
I thought, "Damn, how bad
did I screw up my taxes?"

00:01:11.634 --> 00:01:13.234
But I had an absolute blast.

00:01:13.234 --> 00:01:15.501
Plus, good news --
during the egg hunt,

00:01:15.501 --> 00:01:18.200
I found Trump's missing
call logs from January 6th.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.033 --> 00:01:21.567
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:21.567 --> 00:01:23.334
I found them.

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:25.634
[ Applause ]

00:01:25.634 --> 00:01:27.534
I really did have the best time.

00:01:27.534 --> 00:01:29.701
Do we have a photo of me
with the president?

00:01:29.701 --> 00:01:33.234
Yeah, unbelievable.
It was great.

00:01:33.234 --> 00:01:36.901
Actually, I read my book
"Nana Loves You More"

00:01:36.901 --> 00:01:38.934
to all the kids.
Yeah, and --

00:01:38.934 --> 00:01:39.834
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:39.834 --> 00:01:41.133
With the president

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:43.434
and the first lady
right next to me.

00:01:43.434 --> 00:01:45.601
This is a real photo of this
from this morning. Yeah.

00:01:45.601 --> 00:01:47.033
[ Audience awws ]
Yeah.

00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:49.601
While I was reading to the kids,
the first lady was so sweet.

00:01:49.601 --> 00:01:51.634
She was like, "Sound it out,
Jimmy. You can do it."

00:01:53.267 --> 00:01:54.868
Meanwhile,
I saw that, for Easter,

00:01:54.868 --> 00:01:59.133
a photo of some knockoff
Dollar Store Peeps went viral.

00:01:59.133 --> 00:02:00.701
So it's Dollar Store Peeps.

00:02:00.701 --> 00:02:02.834
Take a look at these things,
this photo.

00:02:02.834 --> 00:02:04.767
Wow.
-Oh.

00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:07.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.334 --> 00:02:10.100
-Looks like Peeps that appeared
in an episode of "Botched."

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:11.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.501 --> 00:02:13.634
Looks like "The Real Housewives
of Marshmallowy Hills."

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:17.200
Let's switch gears.
As you hopefully already know,

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.100
today is tax day.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:21.901
That's right. It's tax day.
Did you know that?

00:02:21.901 --> 00:02:23.167
[ Scattered reaction ]

00:02:23.167 --> 00:02:24.767
Alright. It was kind of
a non-reaction, though.

00:02:24.767 --> 00:02:26.534
Like, "Yeah, uh, okay."

00:02:26.534 --> 00:02:30.200
Yeah, it is tax day,
it's a pandemic, it's spring.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:32.334
So you can get taxed,
vaxxed, and waxed.

00:02:32.334 --> 00:02:35.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:37.234
You can tell it's tax day
'cause right now

00:02:37.234 --> 00:02:39.868
every billionaire
is laying low in space.

00:02:39.868 --> 00:02:41.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.767 --> 00:02:43.234
Well, ahead of today's
tax deadline,

00:02:43.234 --> 00:02:45.534
the White House released
the Bidens' tax return,

00:02:45.534 --> 00:02:48.968
and, together,
they earned over $600,000.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.000
Making Joe Biden

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.033
the Jeff Bezos
of Wilmington, Delaware.

00:02:52.033 --> 00:02:53.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.901 --> 00:02:56.501
Yep, the President made money
from his salary, his book sales,

00:02:56.501 --> 00:02:58.968
and his upcoming cameo
in "Magic Mike 3."

00:03:00.434 --> 00:03:01.934
Well, according
to their tax return,

00:03:01.934 --> 00:03:04.334
the Bidens did not receive
a refund this year.

00:03:05.734 --> 00:03:08.334
When he saw, even Biden
was like, "Friggin' Biden."

00:03:08.334 --> 00:03:10.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.434 --> 00:03:14.901
[ Applause ]

00:03:14.901 --> 00:03:16.100
"Unbelievable."

00:03:18.367 --> 00:03:20.300
But this is cool --
the FDA just authorized

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:23.367
the first ever
COVID breath test.

00:03:23.367 --> 00:03:24.934
It's more than 90% effective.

00:03:24.934 --> 00:03:27.067
Check out what this
breathalyzer looks like.

00:03:27.067 --> 00:03:28.968
This is real.
Yeah.

00:03:28.968 --> 00:03:31.067
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.067 --> 00:03:33.100
-It's amazing.
The guy combined luggage

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.133
with a Capri Sun.
Ah, it's amazing.

00:03:36.567 --> 00:03:39.868
Now there's nasal swabs
and breathalyzers,

00:03:39.868 --> 00:03:42.100
which means pretty soon
you'll see two lines at CVS,

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:44.334
one that says, "Up Yours,"
the other one says, "Blow Me."

00:03:44.334 --> 00:03:46.434
-Hey! Whoa!

00:03:46.434 --> 00:03:48.901
[ Rimshot ]
Whoa!

00:03:48.901 --> 00:03:50.834
Whoa!
[ Applause ]

00:03:50.834 --> 00:03:52.667
Whoa!

00:03:52.667 --> 00:03:53.968
-Well, here in New York today

00:03:53.968 --> 00:03:56.834
former Mayor Michael Bloomberg
spoke at City Hall

00:03:56.834 --> 00:03:58.200
and people were saying
that his mask

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:00.667
seemed too tight for his face.

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:01.934
Look at this.

00:04:01.934 --> 00:04:04.200
-But, seriously,
I was glad to have the chance

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:07.501
to welcome back each of my
predecessors to City Hall

00:04:07.501 --> 00:04:08.534
and I'm glad that you're
-You can see his lips.

00:04:08.534 --> 00:04:10.467
-carrying on that tradition.

00:04:10.467 --> 00:04:12.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.834 --> 00:04:15.734
-He spoke for about 10 more
seconds then passed out.

00:04:15.734 --> 00:04:18.267
Can we see that again?
Yeah.

00:04:18.267 --> 00:04:20.868
It's like in his mouth.

00:04:20.868 --> 00:04:22.434
[ Mumbling ]

00:04:22.434 --> 00:04:23.501
Who makes his mask?

00:04:23.501 --> 00:04:24.868
Lululemon makes his mask.

00:04:24.868 --> 00:04:28.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:30.434
-Oh, boy.
-You know that under that mask,

00:04:30.434 --> 00:04:31.968
he looked like
a Dollar Store Peep. Yeah...

00:04:33.767 --> 00:04:37.234
[ Muffled shouting ]

00:04:37.234 --> 00:04:38.901
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:04:38.901 --> 00:04:40.667
Well, guys, everyone's
talking about this.

00:04:40.667 --> 00:04:42.567
A federal judge has overruled

00:04:42.567 --> 00:04:46.067
the CDC's mask mandate
for planes

00:04:46.067 --> 00:04:47.868
and now all the major airlines

00:04:47.868 --> 00:04:50.634
have dropped their
mask requirements.

00:04:50.634 --> 00:04:52.000
But don't worry,
to keep everyone safe,

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:54.534
you can now bring only
up to 3.4 ounces

00:04:54.534 --> 00:04:55.467
of COVID onboard.

00:04:55.467 --> 00:04:57.200
-Oh.
-That's correct.

00:04:57.200 --> 00:05:00.667
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:02.501
To put it another way,
airlines are basically

00:05:02.501 --> 00:05:04.033
turning off the seatbelt sign
for COVID

00:05:04.033 --> 00:05:05.968
and telling it to move freely
about the cabin.

00:05:05.968 --> 00:05:07.934
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.934 --> 00:05:09.534
Yeah, if you thought
Omicron was bad,

00:05:09.534 --> 00:05:11.367
wait till you meet
the Spirit variant.

00:05:11.367 --> 00:05:14.534
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.534 --> 00:05:15.934
Whoo!
-Whoo!

00:05:15.934 --> 00:05:18.067
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:22.400
-When the news broke,

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:25.100
some pilots actually
announced the news midflight,

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:26.801
and people started celebrating.

00:05:26.801 --> 00:05:28.000
This is true.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:30.133
Yeah, passengers were dancing,
hugging, kissing,

00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:31.634
and now they're all
in quarantine.

00:05:31.634 --> 00:05:33.467
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.467 --> 00:05:36.000
Yeah, there was a crazy scene
on American Airlines.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:37.300
People tore off their masks

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:39.133
and shoved them
right into the ashtrays.

00:05:39.133 --> 00:05:40.300
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:42.534
How old is this plane?
Yeah.

00:05:42.534 --> 00:05:44.067
And it's not just planes.

00:05:44.067 --> 00:05:46.934
Amtrak has also ended
their mask mandate.

00:05:46.934 --> 00:05:48.834
Right now train conductors
are celebrating

00:05:48.834 --> 00:05:51.200
by punching 25 tiny holes
in their masks.

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:55.133
[ Imitates punch clicking ]
[ Laughter ]

00:05:55.133 --> 00:05:56.801
"Can I have your mask, please?"
[ Imitates punch clicking ]

00:05:56.801 --> 00:05:58.334
[ Light laughter ]

00:05:58.334 --> 00:05:59.934
Right now also Uber
has announced

00:05:59.934 --> 00:06:02.100
that they're dropping
all mask requirements.

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:03.200
Honestly, I'm going to miss

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:05.033
getting into a masked
stranger's car.

00:06:05.033 --> 00:06:06.801
It was kind of fun
to play that game --

00:06:06.801 --> 00:06:08.400
my ride to the airport
or kidnapping?

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:10.767
You know?
[ Laughter ]

00:06:10.767 --> 00:06:13.100
Meanwhile, the White House
isn't happy with the ruling.

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:14.667
They called it disappointing

00:06:14.667 --> 00:06:17.000
and urged travelers
to keep wearing masks,

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:19.267
but they said that they're
not fighting the decision.

00:06:19.267 --> 00:06:20.434
It's kind of like your parents

00:06:20.434 --> 00:06:22.133
when you tell them
about your new tattoo.

00:06:22.133 --> 00:06:23.834
[ Laughter ]
"I don't know if you're going

00:06:23.834 --> 00:06:25.667
to like 'Suite Life
of Zack and Cody' in 20 years.

00:06:25.667 --> 00:06:28.868
But go for it.
Get the tattoo.

00:06:28.868 --> 00:06:30.801
Hope for a reunion."

00:06:30.801 --> 00:06:32.000
Speaking of the White House,

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:33.100
I read that President Biden

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:34.834
has told former President Obama

00:06:34.834 --> 00:06:39.000
that he plans to run
for reelection in 2024.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:40.801
Biden was like,
"I'll consider the long,

00:06:40.801 --> 00:06:42.567
silent stare your blessing."

00:06:42.567 --> 00:06:45.267
[ Laughter ]

00:06:54.801 --> 00:06:56.934
Yeah, that was a good one.
Yeah, that's a good joke.

00:06:56.934 --> 00:06:59.234
[ Cheering and applause ]
Thank you.

00:07:01.033 --> 00:07:02.667
Obama actually had
some good advice.

00:07:02.667 --> 00:07:04.334
He was like, "Be careful.
After two terms,

00:07:04.334 --> 00:07:05.834
people might say you look old."

00:07:05.834 --> 00:07:07.834
[ Laughter ]

00:07:07.834 --> 00:07:09.234
Hey, you guys see this?

00:07:09.234 --> 00:07:12.567
French President Emmanuel Macron
is running for reelection,

00:07:12.567 --> 00:07:14.501
and a photo of him
is going viral

00:07:14.501 --> 00:07:16.868
'cause he's showing
a ton of chest hair.

00:07:16.868 --> 00:07:18.534
Take a look.

00:07:18.534 --> 00:07:19.934
[ Laughter ]
-Oh.

00:07:19.934 --> 00:07:21.834
-Yeah.
There he is.

00:07:21.834 --> 00:07:23.100
Well, it's inspired Macron

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:25.033
to test some new
campaign slogans.

00:07:25.033 --> 00:07:26.000
Check these out.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:26.667
First up, there's...

00:07:30.567 --> 00:07:31.934
Next up, there's...

00:07:34.701 --> 00:07:37.467
-Whoa!

00:07:37.467 --> 00:07:38.734
-And finally, there's...

00:07:41.734 --> 00:07:43.334
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:07:43.334 --> 00:07:44.567
Hey!
-Oh!

00:07:44.567 --> 00:07:47.167
-Hey!

00:07:47.167 --> 00:07:49.501
-Macron.

00:07:49.501 --> 00:07:52.167
-Apparently the people of France
love the photo

00:07:52.167 --> 00:07:53.767
and it's become very popular.

00:07:53.767 --> 00:07:56.801
I guess that explains
what I saw earlier today.

00:07:56.801 --> 00:08:01.000
-E15 is about 10 cents a gallon
cheaper than E10.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:02.968
And some gas stations
are offering...

00:08:02.968 --> 00:08:06.767
[ Laughter ]

00:08:06.767 --> 00:08:08.300
-It works.

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:09.567
I like it.

00:08:09.567 --> 00:08:12.300
Approval rating up.
-Yeah.

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:13.734
-Some more news.

00:08:13.734 --> 00:08:15.968
Former President Trump
just released a statement

00:08:15.968 --> 00:08:17.968
saying that Russia and Ukraine
should try

00:08:17.968 --> 00:08:20.367
to reach an agreement
to end the war.

00:08:20.367 --> 00:08:22.801
[ Light laughter ]

00:08:22.801 --> 00:08:24.100
When they heard that,

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:26.334
Miss America contestants
were like, "Nailed it."

00:08:26.334 --> 00:08:29.400
Yeah.
Great answer.

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:31.534
Yep, Trump was like,
"After eight weeks,

00:08:31.534 --> 00:08:34.801
I've now come to realize
this is a no bueno."

00:08:34.801 --> 00:08:36.634
[ Laughter ]

00:08:38.801 --> 00:08:40.601
Switching gears,
this is interesting.

00:08:40.601 --> 00:08:43.000
Scientists in Japan
came up with a creative way

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:44.934
to get people to eat less salt.

00:08:44.934 --> 00:08:46.367
Check this out.

00:08:46.367 --> 00:08:50.501
-Researchers in Japan hope their
new taste-enhancing chopsticks

00:08:50.501 --> 00:08:53.934
will make healthy food
low in salt taste better.

00:08:53.934 --> 00:08:56.100
The high-tech utensils
are hooked up

00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:59.167
to a special computer device
on the user's wrist,

00:08:59.167 --> 00:09:02.167
which causes
a small electric current

00:09:02.167 --> 00:09:04.167
to flow
through what they're eating,

00:09:04.167 --> 00:09:06.167
activating any sodium ions

00:09:06.167 --> 00:09:09.801
and allowing for their tongue
to taste more salt

00:09:09.801 --> 00:09:11.667
than is actually in the food.

00:09:11.667 --> 00:09:14.367
[ Light laughter ]

00:09:14.367 --> 00:09:16.467
-Wow, it's just that simple!

00:09:16.467 --> 00:09:18.434
[ Laughter ]

00:09:18.434 --> 00:09:21.534
Anyone else see a problem
combining soup and electricity?

00:09:21.534 --> 00:09:22.968
[ Laughter ]

00:09:22.968 --> 00:09:24.968
If you want to save time, just
pour the soup over your head

00:09:24.968 --> 00:09:27.601
and plug yourself into a wall.

00:09:27.601 --> 00:09:29.601
I heard about a woman
in Massachusetts

00:09:29.601 --> 00:09:32.033
who was learning to drive
in a cemetery

00:09:32.033 --> 00:09:34.200
and crashed
into eight headstones.

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:35.901
[ Light laughter ]

00:09:35.901 --> 00:09:38.067
It's just weird that her
driving instructor was like,

00:09:38.067 --> 00:09:40.367
"Try a U-turn at Edna Doyle's
final resting place

00:09:40.367 --> 00:09:43.934
and then parallel park
by the mausoleum."

00:09:43.934 --> 00:09:45.968
Yep. So between that and getting
stuck behind a booth,

00:09:45.968 --> 00:09:47.100
she had a real tough day.

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:48.801
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:09:48.801 --> 00:09:50.434
Well, guys, everyone
is talking about this.

00:09:50.434 --> 00:09:51.834
Netflix just announced that,

00:09:51.834 --> 00:09:53.934
for the first time
in over a decade,

00:09:53.934 --> 00:09:57.801
they lost subscribers,
and now their stock is crashing.

00:09:57.801 --> 00:09:59.000
-Ooh.
-Yeah.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:00.334
Not only did
their stock plummet,

00:10:00.334 --> 00:10:02.334
but it turns out that all
the cash they had in the bank

00:10:02.334 --> 00:10:03.400
was just cake.

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:07.567
[ Laughter ]

00:10:07.567 --> 00:10:10.067
Yeah, apparently raising
their subscription fee

00:10:10.067 --> 00:10:11.701
every eight seconds
wasn't such a good idea.

00:10:13.267 --> 00:10:14.968
Right now Netflix
is so desperate for money,

00:10:14.968 --> 00:10:17.267
they're now Googling "Is there
a real life 'Squid Game'?"

00:10:17.267 --> 00:10:19.567
It's sad.

00:10:19.567 --> 00:10:21.000
Netflix is blaming their losses

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:23.767
on fierce competition,
inflation, and Russia.

00:10:25.467 --> 00:10:27.033
When he heard that,
President Biden was like,

00:10:27.033 --> 00:10:28.934
"Hey, get your own excuses.
That's..."

00:10:30.734 --> 00:10:32.901
But now Netflix says
they're open to launching

00:10:32.901 --> 00:10:35.467
lower-priced streaming plans
with ads.

00:10:35.467 --> 00:10:38.467
[ Audience groans ]

00:10:38.467 --> 00:10:40.334
That's right.
Entertainment with commercials.

00:10:40.334 --> 00:10:43.067
It's an innovative new concept
called "television."

00:10:43.067 --> 00:10:44.901
Very interesting.

00:10:44.901 --> 00:10:46.501
Yep, Netflix is losing money.

00:10:46.501 --> 00:10:48.601
You can tell it's having
an effect on all of their shows.

00:10:48.601 --> 00:10:51.234
For instance, "Emily in Paris"
is now

00:10:51.234 --> 00:10:53.567
"Emily in Pittsburgh."
-Oh.

00:10:53.567 --> 00:10:55.501
-It's still good, but, yeah.
-Wow.

00:10:55.501 --> 00:10:57.934
-Also, "The Crown" is now

00:10:57.934 --> 00:10:58.868
"The Hat."

00:11:01.734 --> 00:11:03.834
And finally, "Bridgerton" is now

00:11:03.834 --> 00:11:05.767
